“And you will know the truth, and the truth will set you free.” — John 8:32

But there’s another layer to it.

The truth doesn’t always make you comfortable. Sometimes it destroys the very illusions that made you feel safe.

Truth gives you the freedom to see reality as it is, rather than as you’ve been taught, conditioned, or persuaded to see it.

And once you see clearly, you can choose deliberately.

Knowledge is power. Understanding is leverage. Wisdom is knowing what to do with both.

But freedom also means being willing to discover that you were wrong.

That’s how you keep getting closer to the truth.

